{"id":2415,"slug":"paisan","title":"Paisan","year":1946,"country":"Estonia, Italy","duration":126,"spine":498,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/2415-paisan","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/7b27c9719b8fe36e334fa0ba43910a0e/GwB3ma4IYcYsr5CZ4ZizQW0i0mxyxc_large.jpg","description":"Roberto Rossellini’s follow-up to his breakout Rome Open City was the ambitious, enormously moving Paisan, which consists of six episodes set during the liberation of Italy at the end of World War II, and taking place across the country, from Sicily to the northern Po valley. With its documentary-like visuals and intermingled cast of actors and nonprofessionals, Italians and their American liberators, this look at the struggles of different cultures to communicate and of people to live their everyday lives in extreme circumstances is equal parts charming sentiment and vivid reality. A long-missing treasure of Italian cinema, Paisan is available here in its full original release version.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Roberto Rossellini","slug":"roberto-rossellini"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Carmela Sazio","role":"Carmela","slug":"carmela-sazio"},{"actor":"Robert Van Loon","role":"Joe (first episode)","slug":"robert-van-loon"},{"actor":"Dots M. Johnson","role":"Joe (second episode)","slug":"dots-m-johnson"},{"actor":"Alfonsino Bovino","role":"Pasquale","slug":"alfonsino-bovino"},{"actor":"Maria Michi","role":"Francesca","slug":"maria-michi"},{"actor":"Gar Moore","role":"Fred","slug":"gar-moore"},{"actor":"Harriet White","role":"Harriet","slug":"harriet-white"},{"actor":"Renzo Avanzo","role":"Massimo","slug":"renzo-avanzo"},{"actor":"Bill Tubbs","role":"Captain Bill Martin","slug":"bill-tubbs"},{"actor":"Father Vincenzo Carrella","role":"Friar guardian","slug":"father-vincenzo-carrella"},{"actor":"Captain Owen Jones","role":"Protestant chaplain","slug":"captain-owen-jones"},{"actor":"Sergeant Elmer Feldman","role":"Jewish chaplain","slug":"sergeant-elme